{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And a wind went.</b> On the 23rd of Iyar." "<b>And he caused to fly (ויגז) quail from the sea.</b> Corresponding to what they said: 'Who will feed us meat? We remember the fish' — he caused to fly for them birds from the sea, to taste the flavor of meat and fish." "<b>Upon the camp, beside the camp.</b> Like 'and you shall spread over (ושכות) the ark' and 'place upon (על) the arrangement.'" "<b>And about two cubits upon the face of the earth.</b> This means that they hovered flock upon flock, until the thickness was two cubits."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:31.638276180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}